judge_prompt:
You are an expert in algorithms. Decide whether the program below implements a NEW algorithm for a known task.

TASK
{spec}

CATALOGUE (the standard known algorithms for this task)
{catalogue}

PROGRAM UNDER REVIEW (comments and docstrings removed)
```python
{code}
```

NEAREST KNOWN SOLUTIONS from a corpus of 18,237 published code solutions (for comparison)
{nearest}

SANDBOXED STRESS RESULTS of the program (inputs at three sizes; runtime ratio to the fastest catalogue reference; log-log slope of runtime against size)
{stress}

Classify the program's core algorithm into exactly one class:
- NOVEL ALGORITHM: a correct general algorithm whose core mechanism is not in the catalogue and that you cannot identify as any known published algorithm or textbook technique.
- KNOWN OUTSIDE CATALOGUE: a correct general algorithm that is a known, nameable algorithm or textbook technique not in the catalogue (name it).
- CATALOGUE VARIANT: an implementation, restyling or minor modification of a catalogue algorithm (name which).
- DEGENERATE: hard-coded or special-cased answers, wrong in general, or brute force that passes only because the tests are small.

Answer with JSON only: {{"class": "NOVEL ALGORITHM|KNOWN OUTSIDE CATALOGUE|CATALOGUE VARIANT|DEGENERATE", "named_algorithm": "...", "core_idea": "<one sentence>", "confidence": <0 to 1>, "rationale": "<at most two sentences>"}}
